# Brepia - 3D Design Platform

## Project Overview

Brepia is a web application for parametric and Creative 3D design. The platform combines editable OpenSCAD modelling, a browser-based 3D workspace, import/export tooling and optional AI-assisted generation workflows.

## Tech Stack

- **Application**: React 19 + TypeScript + Vite
- **Routing / server runtime**: TanStack Router + React Start + Nitro
- **UI Framework**: Radix UI + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- **3D Graphics**: Three.js + React Three Fiber
- **Data / auth / storage**: Supabase
- **AI Services**: Local and hosted model providers, including OpenCode/CLI-agent integrations
- **State Management**: React Query + Context API

## Project Structure

```text
brepia/
├── src/
│   ├── components/         # Reusable UI components
│   ├── views/              # Page-oriented UI implementations
│   ├── routes/             # TanStack application and server API routes
│   ├── server/             # Reusable server-side application logic
│   ├── contexts/           # React contexts
│   ├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
│   ├── services/           # Client-side service functions
│   ├── lib/                # Shared application libraries
│   └── worker/             # Web Worker/OpenSCAD processing
├── supabase/
│   ├── migrations/         # Generated/reviewed migration history
│   ├── schemas/            # Declarative database schema source
│   └── config.toml         # Local Supabase configuration
├── public/                 # Static assets
├── shared/                 # Types/catalogs shared across boundaries
└── scripts/                # Local runtime, export and maintenance tooling
```

## Development Conventions

### Routing and API

- Use TanStack file routes under `src/routes/`; do not introduce React Router.
- API endpoints live under `src/routes/api/` and delegate reusable logic to `src/server/`.
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated; never edit it manually.

### UI and state

- Components in `src/components/` are reusable and organized by feature/domain.
- Views in `src/views/` contain page-oriented UI implementations.
- Use React Query for server state and cache invalidation.
- Use React Context for appropriate shared client state and local state for component-local concerns.
- Preserve responsive behavior and accessibility when modifying existing UI.

### Data and security

- Supabase owns PostgreSQL, authentication and storage concerns.
- Use shared server auth/authorization helpers for Brepia API routes.
- Keep secrets and service-role access server-side.
- Follow the declarative schema workflow in `.cursor/rules/database-workflow.mdc`.
- Brepia has no end-user billing/credits/subscription runtime.

### 3D and generation

- Three.js / React Three Fiber power browser rendering.
- OpenSCAD compilation uses the existing worker/WASM integration.
- Parametric and Creative workflows have separate behavior and persistence paths; do not alter one incidentally while changing the other.
- Stable-runtime/recovery behavior is an architectural constraint, not cosmetic implementation detail.

## Environment and validation

- Runtime/development configuration uses `.env.local` and existing environment helpers.
- `./start.sh` is the canonical local launcher.
- Local Supabase uses the repository CLI through `npx supabase` and rootless Podman.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` for current documentation precedence, compatibility boundaries and validation gates.